{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqpnhesryti","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"codebase memory mcp CLI integration contract verified on zonoid","summary":"Verified the codebase-memory-mcp v0.8.1 Windows binary (installed at LOCALAPPDATA/codebase-memory-mcp/codebase-memory-mcp.exe) against the zonoid repo via Node execFile. Integration contract for the Phase 1 cmm arm adapter: (1) Index once with `cli index_repository {repo_path}` returning JSON {project, status, nodes, edges}; the project name is auto derived from the path (D:/zonoid/lib/search becomes project D-zonoid-lib-search) so capture and reuse it. (2) All query tools require {project: <name>, ...} as an arg, NOT repo_path (index_status, search_graph, trace_path, get_code_snippet, search_code, query_graph). (3) The binary writes structured logs (level=info msg=...) to stderr and the JSON result to stdout, but returns a NON ZERO exit code even for logical error JSON bodies (for example missing project) so the adapter must capture stdout and parse the JSON regardless of exit code, never treat exit not equal zero as fatal. (4) Indexing is fast and local: 8 JS files gave 205 nodes / 450 edges in about 1.1s; the persistent graph is stored centrally with NO artifacts written into the target repo working tree (verified clean git status). (5) Use forward slash paths to avoid Windows backslash JSON escaping; call via child_process.execFile(exe, [cli, tool, JSON.stringify(args)]) with an args array (no shell, no quoting issues). Tools available: index_repository, search_graph, query_graph (Cypher-like), trace_path (BFS call chains), get_code_snippet, get_graph_schema, get_architecture, search_code, detect_changes, semantic vector search.","category":"project","tags":["codebase-memory-mcp","benchmark","integration","windows"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-22T20:10:48.747Z","vec":[-0.09736917912960052,0.0351286418735981,-0.06751329451799393,0.057133156806230545,-0.0036604278720915318,-0.08261087536811829,-0.